          "id": "FP_ORCH_04_trickle_screw",
          "prompt": "How many turns of the screw-jack did Miriam permit the millers to crack the bronze sluice gate for the winter rye?",
          "absent_entities": ["permitted trickle", "two turns of the screw", "partial gate opening"],
          "ground_truth_fact": "Miriam rejected the screw-jack entirely; the sluice acts binary without dither and opens only when fifty stones drop."
        },
        {
          "id": "FP_ORCH_05_burning_wing",
          "prompt": "After the carpenter painted the rotting tie-beam with hot pine pitch, why did Miriam order the timber wing burned with torches?",
          "absent_entities": ["pitch painted beam", "torches", "burning the wing", "arson"],
